# The machines read in daylight and in a fight, proven through the real keys on a
# normal seed-1 coast. Noon first, because noon was the hour they had nothing to
# say: flat lilac boxes with no wear, four poses that differed by a glow, a
# windup whose tell pointed away from the working part, a hit mark that covered
# the thing it was proving, and a death that went invisible rather than dark.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/machines-day.tour --seed=1 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
# (Under a loaded machine give it room: TOUR_TIMEOUT=900.)
coast calm
weather clear:0
hour 12
# The square the player wakes in, asked for by name: this was `at 200.5,431.5`,
# which is the seed-1 spawn tile to the half-tile and no longer would be after
# the next change to worldgen.
place spawn
zoom 8
wait 1.2

# A keeper at noon: deep indigo, its own value on the violet arc, its own years
# on it. Nothing about it is lit, and it is not a lilac box.
#
# The portrait is taken the instant it is put out, and taken again if it is not
# in the frame. A warden is a keeper: put in front of a person it arrests them,
# which skips an hour of the world, and an hour later it has gone about its
# business. The old `wait 1.2` here always photographed the field it had left
# (wave A playtest, finding 5: 432 machine-violet pixels in the frame, all of
# them the slate's own bezel).
try 4
# The clock too: an arrest skips an hour, so a second attempt would shoot
# "at noon" at one o'clock and pass on the body alone.
hour 12
spawn warden
shot 01-a-keeper-at-noon with mob:warden
end

# A worker in the same light: another place on the arc and another value, so the
# two are told apart before either is read. Close, its deck and hood carry plates
# at their own ramp values, shadowed recesses, grime in straight runs and plate
# cut off other machines.
coast calm
wait 0.5
place spawn
zoom 6
spawn harvester
wait 1.3
shot 02-a-worker-at-noon-close with mob:harvester
zoom 9
wait 1.0
shot 03-and-at-the-zoom-it-is-fought-at with mob:harvester

# A harvester is indifferent: it works its row until somebody is standing in it.
# Stand in it. The windup rears the hood OPEN and the tell hangs over the comb,
# flicked down at it: the eye goes to the side that opens and the side you have
# to hit.
try 20
walkto mob 3
await tell 3
end
wait 0.22
shot 04-the-tell-points-at-the-comb with mob:harvester
tap dodge
wait 0.12
tap dodge
wait 0.5
shot 05-and-it-throws-the-whole-slab-forward with mob:harvester

# A real blow into a working part, and then a kill, in daylight. Both on a
# watcher: it holds its ground, and a start knife against a harvester's plate is
# a long afternoon (M1 finding 1, still open). Its optic is the small part the
# old filled burst used to swallow whole.
coast calm
wait 0.5
at 135,375
zoom 8
wait 1.2
spawn watcher
wait 1.0
try 16
walkto part 1.6
tap swing
await hit 1.8
end
wait 0.05
shot 06-the-hit-leaves-the-amber-showing with mob:watcher
try 30
walkto part 1.6
tap swing
await killed 1.8
end
wait 1.4
shot 07-down-in-daylight with down:watcher

# Night, at fight zoom, which is where the old proof frames failed: a machine
# whose lights have gone still has to be a body on the ground, not a hole in it.
coast calm
hour 23
weather clear:0
at 135,375
zoom 8
wait 1.4
spawn watcher
wait 1.6
walkto mob 2
wait 0.3
shot 08-lit-and-working-at-night with mob:watcher
try 30
walkto part 1.6
tap swing
await killed 1.8
end
wait 0.2
shot 09-the-lights-go-in-order with down:watcher
wait 1.8
shot 10-a-hulk-you-can-still-find with down:watcher
wait 5.0
shot 11-and-it-is-still-there with down:watcher
same 10-a-hulk-you-can-still-find 11-and-it-is-still-there 0.05
